turns out battlefield one has a game  mode other than conquest no surprise  there at e3 dice showed off a mode not  new to the series called domination and  it's still just as straightforward two  teams fight to hold capture flags  holding a flag generates tickets the  more flags your team holds the more  tickets your team breaks in basically  its infantry only conquest on a smaller  map and there's really not much else to  it capture defend sure it comes off as a  planned bare-boned experience yet my  main takeaway was a stronger sense of  not just what battlefield once infantry  combat entails but where teamwork and  purpose lies within each class the map  was the same as the one seen in conquest  gameplay Sam Quinton just the town  portion essentially meaning that you're  running into the enemy at practically  every step and if that didn't keep you  on your toes battlefield ones  destructible environment is in full  swing doors walls fences are all  practically unreliable you find yourself  rating cover based on the material used  do I put my life in the hands of a  wooden door or this concrete wall the  choice is obvious and the same  disruption goes hand in hand when you're  chasing that kill oh I see you found a  nice wooden door to hide behind how's  that working out for you in the heat of  the moment you're devoting your precious  time into environmental knowledge if an  enemy is behind would shoot if he's  behind a concrete wall use an anti-tank  grenade and shake things up speaking of  shaking things up battlefield ones  dynamic weather is in full swing here  once that fog rolls in so does the close  quarters combat it's strongly advised  you put away that sniper in favor of a  shoddy or SMG and shotgun fans like  myself will love the fog that fog brings  forth those risky moves like dashing  across the street in order to flank a  foe it's a well-fitting changeup  especially when it occurs at random  aesthetically domination really hits the  soldier chords for me and not just  battlefield 1942 but the world war 2  cinematic grit as a whole yes World War  2 I said it but let's face it this is  what battlefield one is and I'm  personally all for it because it works  so well you get flashbacks of Jackson  from saving private ryan and as a medic  i instinctively dashed under fire to go  for that revived fully comfortable with  the circumstances especially with the  heavy implementation of squads you  weren't just spawning on your teammates  you felt the drive to stick with  typically I place shooters as the  dickish lone wolf but here I strive to  huddle next to my teammate under mg fire  busting open barn doors and clearing  houses couple this with dices superb  sound design you really do feel like  you're living in a breathing war flick  and by the way busting open doors and  clearing houses were easily the most  tense and gripping moments of my entire  play all in all as a game-mode  domination was about as simplistic as it  gets yet my takeaway was a game  traveling back to its familiar roofs  with the occasional sprinkling of new  gimmicks like actually seeing practical  use of the poison gas toss it strapped  on a mask and take down the disoriented  enemy these are the gadgets and  mechanics that will really make  battlefield one stand out at the moment  alpha has showed us its core battlefield  one is a remake of a classic World War 2  shooter thanks for watching and don't  forget to subscribe for more battlefield  one content  you
 

